SHIYUKI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OGURI, KAZUMI</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MUROI TOSHIYUKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>OGURI KAZUMI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MUROI, TOSHIYUKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OGURI, KAZUMI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A continuous casting nozzle for molten steel, characterized in that an inner hole surface layer in contact with molten steel of the continuous casting nozzle comprises a composition consisting of (a) 30 to 84 wt.% of agalmatolite, (b) 15 to 60 wt.% of an aggregate consisting of Al2O3 or an aggregate mainly consisting of Al2O3 and having a melting point of 1800  DEG C or higher and (c) 1 to 10 wt.% of silicon carbide.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne une buse de coulée continue pour acier en fusion, qui se caractérise en ce qu'une couche superficielle d'un orifice interne en contact avec l'acier en fusion de la buse de coulée continue comprend une composition contenant a) 30 à 84 % en poids d'agalmatolite; b) 15 à 60 % en poids d'un agrégat constitué de Al2O3, ou d'un agrégat constitué principalement de Al2O3 et ayant un point de fusion d'au moins 1800  DEG C; et c) 1 à 10 % en poids de carbure de silicium.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copy